Man, that thing is not blowing up back there, huh?

3277
03:02:06,360 --> 03:02:07,480
Oh, here we go.

3278
03:02:07,920 --> 03:02:09,040
I think we've made it.

3279
03:02:09,880 --> 03:02:11,240
This can't go wrong now.

3280
03:02:11,960 --> 03:02:12,780
There's no way.

3281
03:02:13,500 --> 03:02:14,720
This is in the bag.

3282
03:02:19,630 --> 03:02:22,450
Hold on, the question is, will I finish the Explore EVE contract?

3283
03:02:22,950 --> 03:02:24,070
I don't know if this will count.

3284
03:02:25,130 --> 03:02:29,210
I'm not sure if this is only going to count with the original vehicle that you landed with.

3285
03:02:29,290 --> 03:02:30,010
I doubt it, though.

3286
03:02:30,490 --> 03:02:34,110
I'm like 99% sure this is going to work, but there is a chance.

3287
03:02:34,870 --> 03:02:35,750
There is a chance.

3288
03:02:37,790 --> 03:02:38,510
That's all I'm saying.

3289
03:02:46,450 --> 03:02:47,770
Grass... shoots her up!

3290
03:03:07,630 --> 03:03:08,510
There they go.

3291
03:03:14,870 --> 03:03:16,410
Let's take some science while we're here.

3292
03:03:19,410 --> 03:03:20,870
Extend solar panels.

3293
03:03:21,970 --> 03:03:22,910
Wait, there's no sun.

3294
03:03:23,370 --> 03:03:24,190
This was useless.

3295
03:03:25,870 --> 03:03:26,650
Lock the temperature.

3296
03:03:26,950 --> 03:03:27,490
Transmit it.

3297
03:03:28,550 --> 03:03:29,810
Oh wait, we can just keep it, right?

3298
03:03:30,070 --> 03:03:31,110
We can keep the science now.

3299
03:03:32,030 --> 03:03:33,730
Seismic data is not going to be useful here.

3300
03:03:34,810 --> 03:03:35,310
Pressure data.

3301
03:03:35,490 --> 03:03:36,230
Wow, there's nothing there.

3302
03:03:38,090 --> 03:03:38,750
Mystery goo.

3303
03:03:40,470 --> 03:03:40,870
Nothing.

3304
03:03:49,080 --> 03:03:49,640
Alright.

3305
03:03:49,640 --> 03:03:50,820
Wait, what are these trees?

3306
03:03:51,120 --> 03:03:52,060
Oh, they're cacti.

3307
03:03:53,580 --> 03:03:54,760
Like, they look weird.

3308
03:03:59,080 --> 03:04:02,100
Would love to have like little lights on this now, so we can see the surface.

3309
03:04:03,600 --> 03:04:05,000
What is that stuff down there?

3310
03:04:05,720 --> 03:04:06,120
Grass?

3311
03:04:07,860 --> 03:04:09,680
Oh yeah, I think it's tiny patches of grass.

3312
03:04:11,820 --> 03:04:12,220
Yep.

3313
03:04:22,250 --> 03:04:22,810
Yeah!

3314
03:04:22,810 --> 03:04:25,030
I can't believe we finally did that mission.

3315
03:04:25,270 --> 03:04:25,770
That's it.

3316
03:04:26,250 --> 03:04:26,970
Hell yeah.

3317
03:04:28,390 --> 03:04:28,950
Payout.

3318
03:04:29,730 --> 03:04:30,690
Very nice.

3319
03:04:31,530 --> 03:04:32,770
Oh, that's so good.

3320
03:04:33,010 --> 03:04:35,090
I'm gonna do some science here.

3321
03:04:35,290 --> 03:04:36,090
Mystery go time.

3322
03:04:36,270 --> 03:04:37,790
And we also gotta do seismic data.

3323
03:04:39,110 --> 03:04:39,670
Seismic.

3324
03:04:40,950 --> 03:04:47,730
This is the first craft that I have had in the vicinity of another planet that has come home.

3325
03:04:52,170 --> 03:04:52,970
That's awesome.

3326
03:04:57,170 --> 03:04:58,790
That's a whole new achievement right there.

3327
03:05:02,350 --> 03:05:03,950
Hey, 27 science?

3328
03:05:05,670 --> 03:05:08,230
Recovery of a vessel returned from the surface of Gili.

3329
03:05:09,530 --> 03:05:11,390
Wait, that didn't even say that anywhere.

3330
03:05:12,710 --> 03:05:14,150
That's unexpected goodies.

3331
03:05:16,190 --> 03:05:17,110
Very nice.

3332
03:05:19,550 --> 03:05:21,270
Okay, warp to next day.

3333
03:05:21,670 --> 03:05:25,410
Now it's time... to launch the Doona rocket.

3334
03:05:25,530 --> 03:05:30,430
But wait, before we launch the Doona rocket... I'm going to look at the tracking station.

3335
03:05:36,410 --> 03:05:38,150
Oh, it's gonna be a while still.

3336
03:05:38,410 --> 03:05:38,530
Okay.

3337
03:05:39,810 --> 03:05:40,930
Yeah, not yet, not yet.

3338
03:05:41,190 --> 03:05:42,890
Maybe we can do one or two missions in between.

3339
03:05:43,910 --> 03:05:46,710
Somewhere in... the carbon system.

3340
03:05:47,670 --> 03:05:49,310
Let me see what we got on the menu here.

3341
03:05:50,290 --> 03:05:53,970
Volcanic rock, that is... Let me see here.

3342
03:05:54,950 --> 03:05:58,010
You can find one of these in the peaks, craters, or foothill biomes?

3343
03:05:59,490 --> 03:06:00,090
But where?

3344
03:06:02,470 --> 03:06:03,390
Oh, on Eve!

3345
03:06:03,550 --> 03:06:04,410
Okay, this is Eve.

3346
03:06:05,920 --> 03:06:06,760
Atmospheric surveys!

3347
03:06:07,040 --> 03:06:07,280
Yo!

3348
03:06:09,240 --> 03:06:11,700
Oh, I thought it was with the new item I got.

3349
03:06:11,840 --> 03:06:12,020
Damn.

3350
03:06:12,240 --> 03:06:12,700
Okay, never mind.

3351
03:06:13,680 --> 03:06:15,620
Finished construction of a rover on the surface of Minmus.

3352
03:06:16,000 --> 03:06:16,360
Hey!

3353
03:06:16,600 --> 03:06:17,280
You know what?

3354
03:06:17,920 --> 03:06:18,820
We can do that.

3355
03:06:19,260 --> 03:06:27,580
Because then we're gonna take off afterward and go back to the Minmus station, the surface station, and bring the more photovoltaic panels.

3356
03:06:28,040 --> 03:06:29,840
So we can finally do that contract as well.

3357
03:06:29,920 --> 03:06:31,880
We're gonna do both of those at the same time.

3358
03:06:32,480 --> 03:06:33,240
I like it.

3359
03:06:33,610 --> 03:06:34,350
Take that one.

3360
03:06:35,550 --> 03:06:37,450
Position satellite in a polar orbit of Minmus?

3361
03:06:37,730 --> 03:06:38,010
Nah.

3362
03:06:40,610 --> 03:06:41,170
Nah.

3363
03:06:42,050 --> 03:06:43,190
Wait, another Explore EVE.

3364
03:06:43,590 --> 03:06:45,330
Rendezvous two vessels in orbit of EVE.

3365
03:06:45,690 --> 03:06:47,790
Dock two vessels on or around EVE.

3366
03:06:47,890 --> 03:06:48,050
Okay.

3367
03:06:49,710 --> 03:06:52,190
No thanks.

3368
03:06:53,850 --> 03:06:55,310
Now, this is interesting.

3369
03:06:56,190 --> 03:06:58,550
Seismic sensor science from the surface of Minmus.

3370
03:06:58,730 --> 03:06:59,750
Isn't that an easy W?

3371
03:07:00,150 --> 03:07:01,590
I feel like I already have that.

3372
03:07:05,330 --> 03:07:06,310
Repair a satellite.

3373
03:07:07,290 --> 03:07:09,710
I mean, that one we can do on our way to Menmus.

3374
03:07:10,570 --> 03:07:10,810
Yep.

3375
03:07:13,270 --> 03:07:18,250
Detect three comets with a Sentinel Infrared Telescope.

3376
03:07:20,270 --> 03:07:24,110
Finding a comet is an astronomer's dream since the early days of stargazing.

3377
03:07:24,470 --> 03:07:25,870
Now you get to help.

3378
03:07:26,170 --> 03:07:29,130
Discover three comets using the Sentinel Infrared Telescope.

3379
03:07:29,850 --> 03:07:30,230
Ooh.

3380
03:07:31,000 --> 03:07:37,140
The mapping process will happen passively over a length of time as any active sentinels are operating.

3381
03:07:39,040 --> 03:07:39,400
Really?

3382
03:07:39,740 --> 03:07:41,640
They do not need to be newly launched.

3383
03:07:41,960 --> 03:07:45,580
You will receive progress notifications as suitable comets are mapped.

3384
03:07:46,620 --> 03:07:47,140
What?

3385
03:07:48,300 --> 03:07:49,760
Wait, really?

3386
03:07:50,020 --> 03:07:51,460
There's actually comets?

3387
03:07:55,040 --> 03:07:56,300
But not really, though, right?

3388
03:07:57,500 --> 03:08:01,360
It's gonna be like, oh, you detected a comet, but it's not actually a physical object?

3389
03:08:03,840 --> 03:08:04,360
I guess?

3390
03:08:05,020 --> 03:08:10,720
I don't know, that's my prediction, but I just... I feel like it wouldn't be... something that this game would do, you know?

3391
03:08:10,880 --> 03:08:15,840
We just have these sort of... comets out there, just... hurtling through space, I guess?

3392
03:08:16,680 --> 03:08:20,460
It seems like it's... out of the scope of this game, you know what I mean?

3393
03:08:24,020 --> 03:08:27,560
But I wanted to launch one of these anyway, so... I'll take it.

3394
03:08:29,240 --> 03:08:31,940
Rescue Frohat from the surface of... Frohat?

3395
03:08:32,160 --> 03:08:33,400
What is that name?

3396
03:08:34,860 --> 03:08:35,300
Frohat.

3397
03:08:36,880 --> 03:08:37,820
Come on, man.

3398
03:08:38,600 --> 03:08:41,160
I mean, this is gonna be the ultimate Minmus mission of all time.

3399
03:08:41,980 --> 03:08:44,240
Yeah, we're gonna do... Okay, so check it out.

3400
03:08:44,740 --> 03:08:45,840
This is the mission, alright?

3401
03:08:47,080 --> 03:08:48,380
If you choose to accept it.

3402
03:08:49,720 --> 03:08:51,080
We're going to...

3403
03:08:52,220 --> 03:08:54,160
Launch a vessel from Kirban.

3404
03:08:56,000 --> 03:08:58,640
With... photovoltaic panels in the storage.

3405
03:08:59,500 --> 03:09:03,340
We're then gonna go out... repair a satellite in orbit of Minmus.

3406
03:09:03,880 --> 03:09:08,500
When that is done... we are going to... land on Minmus.

3407
03:09:09,140 --> 03:09:10,740
Finish repairing a rover.

3408
03:09:11,460 --> 03:09:13,600
Then we're gonna take off from Minmus again.

3409
03:09:14,180 --> 03:09:19,300
And we are gonna land... near someone and rescue Frohat.

3410
03:09:20,230 --> 03:09:21,790
And then we're gonna take off again.

3411
03:09:22,690 --> 03:09:26,010
And then we're gonna go to the Minmus station on Minmus.

3412
03:09:26,650 --> 03:09:30,590
Hand over the parts so we can get the science from the surface stuff.

3413
03:09:32,010 --> 03:09:32,930
That's the mission.

3414
03:09:34,790 --> 03:09:36,330
Doesn't that sound amazing?

3415
03:09:37,370 --> 03:09:38,990
Bro, look how rich we are!

3416
03:09:39,790 --> 03:09:41,310
We have almost 2 million.

3417
03:09:41,430 --> 03:09:43,110
Dude, this... Hold on, we gotta save the game.

3418
03:09:43,910 --> 03:09:47,470
This mission... Like, this... I mean...

3419
03:09:47,480 --> 03:09:49,660
This space program is just kicking ass right now.

3420
03:09:50,100 --> 03:09:51,260
Holy shit.

3421
03:09:51,960 --> 03:09:53,960
What should I... Let's do this one.

3422
03:09:54,620 --> 03:09:55,900
New tracking station.

3423
03:09:57,120 --> 03:10:00,520
Max DSN power is 250 G's now.

3424
03:10:01,060 --> 03:10:01,980
Up from 50.

3425
03:10:03,020 --> 03:10:03,680
Damn.

3426
03:10:04,840 --> 03:10:05,200
Yep.

3427
03:10:05,620 --> 03:10:06,360
Thank you.

3428
03:10:06,540 --> 03:10:06,720
Ooh.

3429
03:10:07,860 --> 03:10:08,540
Wow.

3430
03:10:09,300 --> 03:10:13,220
Almost looks like a tiny version of the VLA in New Mexico.

3431
03:10:15,350 --> 03:10:17,470
You just need a couple more along these ways, you know.

3432
03:10:18,390 --> 03:10:19,190
Uh, right?

3433
03:10:19,490 --> 03:10:20,450
Okay, so we did that.

3434
03:10:20,770 --> 03:10:23,230
Now, maneuver tool available.

3435
03:10:25,530 --> 03:10:26,370
What do you mean?

3436
03:10:27,050 --> 03:10:29,110
Is that something we can do when we're flying?

3437
03:10:30,250 --> 03:10:30,990
Or what?

3438
03:10:31,610 --> 03:10:35,390
Let me try... Oh, let me have a look at this rover, I guess.

3439
03:10:41,510 --> 03:10:48,270
Okay, I'm just gonna take a wild guess here and say that I think I know what's missing.

3440
03:10:48,270 --> 03:10:50,010
I can't quite put my finger on it.

3441
03:10:51,050 --> 03:10:55,170
But there is something missing with this rover.

3442
03:10:57,690 --> 03:10:58,210
Right?

3443
03:10:58,810 --> 03:10:59,630
What is it?

3444
03:11:00,230 --> 03:11:01,090
Something's missing.

3445
03:11:02,770 --> 03:11:04,430
Dude, this looks actually really cool.

3446
03:11:04,990 --> 03:11:08,890
Can you imagine being on the surface of Minmus like this and looking up at the stars?

3447
03:11:11,900 --> 03:11:17,640
In fact, let's make a nice little... ending screen here, because I'm gonna stop streaming now.

3448
03:11:18,440 --> 03:11:19,020
Look at that.

3449
03:11:19,140 --> 03:11:23,940
That could be a... If you had the menu over here, that could have been the menu screen.

3450
03:11:26,800 --> 03:11:27,780
We're gonna keep it there.

3451
03:11:29,060 --> 03:11:29,820
What's up, guys?

3452
03:11:32,820 --> 03:11:33,560
How you doing?

3453
03:11:40,020 --> 03:11:41,060
What do you think about that?

3454
03:11:42,700 --> 03:11:43,880
I'm reading chat right now.

3455
03:11:44,120 --> 03:11:45,060
This is the end screen.

3456
03:11:46,080 --> 03:11:48,860
This is so much cooler than my actual end screen.

3457
03:11:52,110 --> 03:11:52,650
Right?

3458
03:11:52,650 --> 03:11:53,690
It's so good.

3459
03:11:55,750 --> 03:11:58,630
With the headlights as well, it's perfect.

3460
03:12:00,710 --> 03:12:02,510
Oh, you guys were clearing chat just now.

3461
03:12:02,750 --> 03:12:05,970
I think I saw one moment where the chat was gone completely.

3462
03:12:06,630 --> 03:12:09,390
So you can definitely extract the screenshot from that.

3463
03:12:12,350 --> 03:12:18,050
I have to say, I think this may have been the most successful session so far in KSP.

3464
03:12:19,970 --> 03:12:20,830
What do you think?

3465
03:12:23,010 --> 03:12:23,810
Ah, okay.

3466
03:12:24,110 --> 03:12:28,550
Maybe the one time I first broke through the clouds on EVE was close.

3467
03:12:29,130 --> 03:12:31,470
Or the Minmus spin slam maneuver.

3468
03:12:32,590 --> 03:12:34,090
That was also pretty good.

3469
03:12:39,540 --> 03:12:42,740
You're at the point where you really should give free IVA another chance.

3470
03:12:43,360 --> 03:12:47,160
Exploring the stations you build and physically moving curbs... Yeah, but it was janky as hell, man.

3471
03:12:50,710 --> 03:12:53,890
I did a very quick test in a testbed environment.

3472
03:12:56,090 --> 03:12:57,430
I just didn't like it that much.

3473
03:12:58,950 --> 03:13:00,470
Maybe I'll give it another shot, okay?

3474
03:13:01,250 --> 03:13:02,290
Okay, let's say this.

3475
03:13:02,390 --> 03:13:04,130
I'll promise to give it another quick shot, okay?

3476
03:13:04,750 --> 03:13:09,130
I'm going to make a... a... what do you call it?

3477
03:13:10,730 --> 03:13:11,510
Yeah, you know what?

3478
03:13:11,510 --> 03:13:16,090
I guess I'm gonna try the research part there and try and move a guy around in there.

3479
03:13:17,960 --> 03:13:19,240
Because we have one already, right?

3480
03:13:19,400 --> 03:13:23,500
Around Moon, so... I'm gonna try and just move around there and see if I like it or not.

3481
03:13:24,800 --> 03:13:25,380
I promise.

3482
03:13:27,640 --> 03:13:29,220
You're currently going through Hollow Knight on YouTube.

3483
03:13:29,340 --> 03:13:30,140
Your videos are so cool.

3484
03:13:30,240 --> 03:13:31,200
Thank you, Witch Slayer!

3485
03:13:32,180 --> 03:13:32,720
Appreciate it.

3486
03:13:33,460 --> 03:13:34,160
Have a good day.

3487
03:13:35,160 --> 03:13:36,780
This could be a good thumbnail for the VOD.

3488
03:13:37,680 --> 03:13:39,700
Yeah, but I gotta keep it consistent, you know?

3489
03:13:39,780 --> 03:13:45,360
I can't just... The thing is, this will be more of a surprise when you watch the video, right?

3490
03:13:45,780 --> 03:13:47,280
You'll reach this point and go, wow.

3491
03:13:49,580 --> 03:13:50,600
But it is a good thumbnail.

3492
03:13:52,440 --> 03:13:55,280
This is the best KSP content I've... Thank you, LogoLeft!

3493
03:13:56,480 --> 03:13:57,280
That's so awesome.

3494
03:13:57,400 --> 03:13:58,060
Thank you for saying that.

3495
03:14:00,100 --> 03:14:02,760
I would say this is also my favorite KSP content.

3496
03:14:03,380 --> 03:14:04,740
Because it's the only one I'm consuming.

3497
03:14:05,460 --> 03:14:06,740
And I'm having a blast with this.

3498
03:14:10,100 --> 03:14:13,560
I have a feeling the Minmus mission is gonna be really challenging.

3499
03:14:13,860 --> 03:14:15,120
The one I'm gonna do next time.

3500
03:14:15,720 --> 03:14:17,840
It's gonna be Minmus mission into Doona.

3501
03:14:18,700 --> 03:14:20,100
Next session is gonna be wild.

3502
03:14:23,330 --> 03:14:25,810
I tried to play KSP because you're making it look easy.

3503
03:14:25,970 --> 03:14:27,350
I'm not getting the same results.

3504
03:14:27,790 --> 03:14:28,430
That's okay.

3505
03:14:29,270 --> 03:14:31,010
I'm also taking my time with it, right?

3506
03:14:31,570 --> 03:14:36,550
Like, when I built my rockets, I spent an insane amount of time in the assembly building.

3507
03:14:38,010 --> 03:14:40,430
And I also have some intuition, you know?

3508
03:14:43,630 --> 03:14:46,590
I sure hope your next Doona vision doesn't end the same as the last one.

3509
03:14:47,110 --> 03:14:47,550
Right?

3510
03:14:48,730 --> 03:14:50,510
We're gonna crash into the moon again.

3511
03:14:57,600 --> 03:14:59,500
You mentioned KSP cinematic films.

3512
03:14:59,600 --> 03:15:03,340
If you ever want to check it out after you're done with this series, check out Sav on KSP.

3513
03:15:03,740 --> 03:15:06,240
He has three medium films on cinematic clips?

3514
03:15:06,740 --> 03:15:07,100
Really?

3515
03:15:08,460 --> 03:15:08,820
Cool.

3516
03:15:09,160 --> 03:15:09,740
You know what?

3517
03:15:09,800 --> 03:15:11,860
I think I would love to make content like that, you know?

3518
03:15:14,060 --> 03:15:20,940
I think I would love to just sit there and clip that together and do the shots and stuff like that, because I'm already kind of doing it while playing.

3519
03:15:21,740 --> 03:15:22,100
Right?

3520
03:15:24,000 --> 03:15:25,540
Like, I'm sort of just...

3521
03:15:25,280 --> 03:15:28,760
Doing it live in a way, like, oh, I'm just enjoying this shot so much.

3522
03:15:28,760 --> 03:15:31,180
I'm just going to keep it on that, you know, for a while while I look at it.

3523
03:15:31,820 --> 03:15:32,500
It's so nice.

3524
03:15:37,750 --> 03:15:38,270
Yeah.

3525
03:15:38,870 --> 03:15:41,590
Like, the amount of mods for this game is crazy.

3526
03:15:42,910 --> 03:15:45,890
I'm so excited for Kitten Space Agency.

3527
03:15:46,110 --> 03:15:47,650
Although it's probably gonna take some years.

3528
03:15:49,610 --> 03:15:50,130
Imagine.

3529
03:15:50,930 --> 03:15:55,070
A modern version or reimagination of this game.

3530
03:15:55,290 --> 03:15:55,710
Right?

3531
03:15:56,770 --> 03:15:58,970
We are definitely playing that when it comes out.

3532
03:15:59,130 --> 03:15:59,830
Holy shit.

3533
03:16:01,630 --> 03:16:06,770
Would you play a co-op game about operating a submarine under the ice of Europa with goofy physics and scary creatures?

3534
03:16:07,250 --> 03:16:10,710
I've actually tried Barotrauma before, just Martani.

3535
03:16:11,290 --> 03:16:15,270
But, like, I've only played the very beginning with my friend, and we didn't really understand what was happening.

3536
03:16:17,810 --> 03:16:20,630
And it seemed interesting enough, but not, like, crazy interesting.

3537
03:16:21,250 --> 03:16:24,050
But maybe it, you know, gets more interesting as you go along.

3538
03:16:32,260 --> 03:16:35,200
How about the Poot Milky Way Skybox mod?

3539
03:16:36,180 --> 03:16:38,960
But this is not the Milky Way, though, is it?

3540
03:16:39,140 --> 03:16:40,120
This is a different universe.

3541
03:16:40,880 --> 03:16:42,100
It's a different reality.

3542
03:16:46,380 --> 03:16:49,440
The modern version of KSP is called Juno New Origins.

3543
03:16:49,760 --> 03:16:51,980
Are you talking about the spacecraft or an actual game?

3544
03:16:54,760 --> 03:16:55,880
Oh, it's a game.

3545
03:16:58,400 --> 03:17:00,140
3D Aerospace Sandbox.

3546
03:17:08,700 --> 03:17:15,280
Oh, it's like a much more realistic game in the sense that it's like humans, you know?

3547
03:17:16,080 --> 03:17:17,340
And the space program and stuff.

3548
03:17:17,520 --> 03:17:18,300
NASA, pretty much.

3549
03:17:25,450 --> 03:17:27,570
I'm very cautiously excited about KSA.

3550
03:17:27,710 --> 03:17:30,370
Sometimes it feels like they're adding way too much real-life stuff.

3551
03:17:31,050 --> 03:17:34,190
Yeah, you should always take all that with a grain of salt, of course.

3552
03:17:34,930 --> 03:17:39,890
I remember... back when they announced Kerbal Space Program 2.

3553
03:17:40,370 --> 03:17:44,670
That was actually when I was like, oh shit, maybe I should start giving this a shot, because the trailer for that looked amazing.

3554
03:17:45,690 --> 03:17:49,390
But then they showed a bunch of promo clips.

3555
03:17:49,950 --> 03:17:52,610
Not of gameplay, but of like...

3556
03:17:53,100 --> 03:17:56,020
Developers talking to the camera with nice lighting and all that, you know?

3557
03:17:56,680 --> 03:17:58,340
And it's always like this.

3558
03:17:58,680 --> 03:18:01,080
When I saw that, I was like, yeah, this game's gonna be trash.

3559
03:18:02,320 --> 03:18:04,660
I knew the first game was, like, famous for being good.

3560
03:18:05,060 --> 03:18:08,660
But I just knew that the second game was gonna be trash as soon as I saw that trailer.

3561
03:18:09,380 --> 03:18:16,480
Because they never show gameplay and always show, you know, the developers talking with nice lighting in these studio environments when they have nothing good to show.

3562
03:18:17,360 --> 03:18:18,480
It's always like that.

3563
03:18:18,520 --> 03:18:19,060
Have you noticed?

3564
03:18:22,600 --> 03:18:25,180
But that's just my, you know, superstition, I guess.

3565
03:18:25,620 --> 03:18:27,080
That's my conspiracy theory.

3566
03:18:29,520 --> 03:18:31,020
Will there be a Season 2 KSP?

3567
03:18:31,100 --> 03:18:32,460
Yeah, it's called KSA, man.

3568
03:18:35,760 --> 03:18:37,720
Actually, maybe there will be a Season 2 KSP.

3569
03:18:38,160 --> 03:18:39,300
Of Kerbal Space Program.

3570
03:18:41,300 --> 03:18:42,740
Maybe with even more mods.

3571
03:18:46,040 --> 03:18:47,520
But it wouldn't be right after this one.

3572
03:18:56,980 --> 03:19:00,580
Yeah, I know... I just thought I'd mention the KSP2 thing.

3573
03:19:00,680 --> 03:19:03,000
I'm not talking about KSA directly.

3574
03:19:03,680 --> 03:19:07,120
I'm just saying be, you know, wary of that stuff.

3575
03:19:13,760 --> 03:19:15,240
KSA looks and runs well, apparently.

3576
03:19:15,440 --> 03:19:19,060
If you have the 12 gigabytes of VRAM needed, otherwise it doesn't boot at all and runs terribly.

3577
03:19:19,520 --> 03:19:21,200
Oh, they need to optimize that.

3578
03:19:21,720 --> 03:19:24,900
I mean, I'm just sitting here laughing in 32 gigabytes of VRAM, right?

3579
03:19:25,320 --> 03:19:28,040
But most people have 8 gigabytes, if not less.

3580
03:19:28,600 --> 03:19:31,180
So that's absolutely not something you want to make.

3581
03:19:31,720 --> 03:19:32,860
You want to reduce that.

3582
03:19:34,480 --> 03:19:38,980
No, this background music is from... Factorio, actually.

3583
03:19:39,160 --> 03:19:40,800
The one you're hearing right now, Toasty Crotch.

3584
03:19:43,150 --> 03:19:44,090
Toasty Crotch.

3585
03:19:44,750 --> 03:19:46,770
How do I pronounce your name correctly?

3586
03:19:47,250 --> 03:19:47,770
Crotchy?

3587
03:19:51,210 --> 03:19:52,270
You have 4 gigabytes?

3588
03:19:52,670 --> 03:19:52,950
Oof.

3589
03:19:53,430 --> 03:19:54,230
In this day and age?

3590
03:19:57,790 --> 03:19:59,850
You play fully modded KSP with 4?

3591
03:20:00,010 --> 03:20:00,230
Damn.

3592
03:20:00,570 --> 03:20:03,950
You must have some... a pretty good and efficient setup going there.

3593
03:20:08,320 --> 03:20:09,020
Greedy AI.

3594
03:20:09,260 --> 03:20:10,540
Stealing all our RAM, man.

3595
03:20:11,840 --> 03:20:12,900
Freaking RAM shortages.

3596
03:20:13,220 --> 03:20:14,520
It's not just RAM, by the way.

3597
03:20:14,680 --> 03:20:16,960
I was looking into getting more storage in general.

3598
03:20:17,500 --> 03:20:19,180
You know, like HDDs.

3599
03:20:19,600 --> 03:20:20,960
Old school tape drives.

3600
03:20:21,700 --> 03:20:24,300
Those things cost a million bucks now, man.

3601
03:20:24,400 --> 03:20:25,660
There's no way I'm buying that now.

3602
03:20:26,260 --> 03:20:27,580
It's way too expensive.

3603
03:20:29,200 --> 03:20:31,940
I said goodbye to that dream real quick when I saw the prices.

3604
03:20:36,410 --> 03:20:37,710
Even CDs?

3605
03:20:38,050 --> 03:20:38,430
No way.

3606
03:20:38,690 --> 03:20:40,890
There's no way CDs are rising in price.

3607
03:20:41,330 --> 03:20:42,830
Who uses CDs?

3608
03:20:43,410 --> 03:20:44,830
That's 700 megabytes.

3609
03:20:44,950 --> 03:20:45,310
Come on.

3610
03:20:46,190 --> 03:20:47,370
That's ridiculous.

3611
03:20:48,050 --> 03:20:50,830
Nobody even has a CD drive nowadays.

3612
03:20:54,940 --> 03:20:56,860
There was one time where storage was cheap.

3613
03:20:57,000 --> 03:20:59,220
Yeah, it's called like two years ago or three years ago.

3614
03:20:59,960 --> 03:21:03,260
Because I bought storage around two or three years ago and it was cheap.

3615
03:21:03,920 --> 03:21:06,500
And I did it right before everything went to shit.

3616
03:21:07,000 --> 03:21:08,920
I'm still so lucky about that, you know?

3617
03:21:16,460 --> 03:21:17,880
Will you have a quantum computer?

3618
03:21:18,020 --> 03:21:19,460
I already have, kinda.

3619
03:21:20,960 --> 03:21:22,540
My computer is pretty good.

3620
03:21:24,000 --> 03:21:24,760
Weird flex.

3621
03:21:26,920 --> 03:21:28,120
I mean, it has to be, right?

3622
03:21:28,180 --> 03:21:35,300
I'm running a single PC setup where I'm playing games in 4K, streaming it in 4K, and recording it in 4K at the same time.

3623
03:21:35,360 --> 03:21:37,380
No, wait, I'm streaming it in 1440p.

3624
03:21:38,080 --> 03:21:40,300
So you kinda need a beefy PC for that.

3625
03:21:44,410 --> 03:21:45,790
Are we getting a WoW stream later?

3626
03:21:45,930 --> 03:21:46,910
You betcha, man!

3627
03:21:48,490 --> 03:21:48,850
Definitely.

3628
03:21:49,170 --> 03:21:50,630
I just gotta go eat some dinner first.

3629
03:21:51,430 --> 03:21:54,290
And maybe chill with my cat a bit, and then we're gonna play some WoW.

3630
03:21:55,370 --> 03:21:59,550
Now that I have my whole setup back up and running, I'm gonna play so many games.

3631
03:22:06,770 --> 03:22:20,830
I mean, yeah, AI bubble... If that's gonna... I mean, if that's what it takes to get the RAM prices and all those things down... It still sucks, though, because it's gonna... Like, a bubble is a bubble, and a bubble is no good for anyone.

3632
03:22:21,530 --> 03:22:26,030
You know, like, if that bursts, it's... A lot of people are gonna lose a lot of money.

3633
03:22:26,110 --> 03:22:26,850
It's never good.

3634
03:22:29,950 --> 03:22:31,690
Maybe punch cards will make a comeback.

3635
03:22:32,610 --> 03:22:35,470
Dude, I'm not even old enough for punch cards.

3636
03:22:35,570 --> 03:22:36,650
How old are you, Dadly?

3637
03:22:37,290 --> 03:22:39,630
Well, the fact that your name is Dadly... Hmm.

3638
03:22:40,350 --> 03:22:41,110
Maybe an indication.

3639
03:22:44,300 --> 03:22:46,640
I did use floppy disks, though, when I was a kid.

3640
03:22:46,820 --> 03:22:47,560
But only briefly.

3641
03:22:47,780 --> 03:22:49,380
CDs started to take over when I was a kid.

3642
03:22:50,420 --> 03:22:52,200
But I do remember having floppies.

3643
03:22:55,000 --> 03:22:57,280
I think it's funny when you stream a Switch game in 4K.

3644
03:22:57,840 --> 03:22:59,020
Why is it funny, Logo?

3645
03:23:00,640 --> 03:23:02,880
It actually produces a better image on YouTube.

3646
03:23:03,120 --> 03:23:07,020
Because YouTube allocates more bitrate to a 4K image.

3647
03:23:07,020 --> 03:23:08,860
Even though the game is not really 4K.

3648
03:23:09,220 --> 03:23:11,560
If you upload it in 4K, it's better on YouTube.

3649
03:23:18,500 --> 03:23:21,540
Also, aren't there games that actually run in 4K on the Switch 2 nowadays?

3650
03:23:22,920 --> 03:23:26,420
I mean, that console can really punch above its weight, right?

3651
03:23:29,700 --> 03:23:32,360
I mean, granted, 30 frames per second, I guess, but still.

3652
03:23:36,140 --> 03:23:38,060
I don't know about the economic stuff.

3653
03:23:38,180 --> 03:23:39,120
I'm not an economist.

3654
03:23:39,280 --> 03:23:39,860
I don't know shit.

3655
03:23:42,740 --> 03:23:44,700
I'm talking out of my ass when it comes to that stuff.

3656
03:23:48,080 --> 03:23:49,920
The browser might run in 4K.

3657
03:23:50,140 --> 03:23:50,700
Oh, okay.

3658
03:23:53,900 --> 03:23:55,460
Oh, so you're not that old again.

3659
03:23:55,600 --> 03:23:55,680
Okay.

3660
03:23:58,280 --> 03:23:59,580
Guys, I'm gonna be out of here.

3661
03:23:59,660 --> 03:23:59,960
Thank you.

3662
03:24:00,020 --> 03:24:01,160
This was an amazing stream.

3663
03:24:01,300 --> 03:24:03,280
It's good to play some more KSP.

3664
03:24:03,740 --> 03:24:06,200
We're gonna get some more KSP in not too long.

3665
03:24:06,740 --> 03:24:09,260
We also have WoW and MC, of course.

3666
03:24:09,780 --> 03:24:13,440
And then GTA 6 is coming out next week!

3667
03:24:13,720 --> 03:24:14,520
Can you believe that?

3668
03:24:15,260 --> 03:24:16,480
Six days from now, I think.

3669
03:24:16,600 --> 03:24:17,440
Six, seven, eight, nine, yeah.

3670
03:24:18,060 --> 03:24:18,780
I'll see you around.

3671
03:24:19,500 --> 03:24:20,380
WoW later tonight.

3672
03:24:20,740 --> 03:24:21,120
Bye-bye.
